Fast Sandbox: evict from the shared image cache by what is on disk

Base: opensandbox-group/fast-sandbox main at 7b28a0c (2026-10-27), the fastlet
OpenSandbox 1.2.0 ships: rebuilding that commit with Go 1.25.14 reproduces the
published binary byte for byte. Apply with `git apply`.

Every fastlet on a node shares one image cache, but its GC ranked eviction by
that fastlet's in-memory use counts, under a 20 GiB limit that holds two 9 GiB
root filesystems. No checkpoint is ever referenced (a paused sandbox has no
state directory and a running one records its template), so the first fastlet
to collect deleted checkpoints it had never used, the newest included, and the
next resume pulled 14 GB again. Boots now leave a marker in the cache entry
that every fastlet can read: spent checkpoints go first, then other entries
oldest first, templates last. FAST_SANDBOX_IMAGE_CACHE_LIMIT_GIB sets the limit.
See docs/research/fast-sandbox-pause-time.md in different-ai/differently.

